														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3881939">
									

<p>I can respect the sheer amount of worldbuilding that goes on here, as you basically build up an entire civilization and its history in this article. However, I'll be blunt in saying that the amount of exposition is a slog to get through, for what is ultimatley the little payoff of a treaty and some modern excerpts.</p>
<p>This article reminds me of the most of the other contest entry Garfield Minus Garfield in its attempt at authenticity. While that article has a great eye for presenting things as historical documents as well as some highly entertaining logs that put a fresh face on historical figures, this article lacks such details and what I would consider the main meat of the article (the Journal) lacks the same pop and energy and in its place has a slow burn.</p>
<p>I can stomach a fair amount of exposition dumping in a piece, but it is the duty of the author to keep the exposition entertaining along the way and make the mountain worth reaching the summit.</p>
<p>-1.</p>

