<p>I've always liked these sorts of lengthy articles with a social studies focus. It's probably the main reason why I'm so much into Sarkicism to begin with.</p>
<p>Locating a band of Sarkites or para-Sarkites in Polynesia is probably one of the more novel takes on the theme. I really like the sovereign polity description, with its flag and form of government and all. Though it does feel a bit hard to believe that such a large polity would still be unknown what with the size of it, I think that's easily fixed by adding a bit about the Foundation scrubbing satellite footage to remove any traces of it.</p>
<p>There are a few spelling errors and odd word choices here and there that I could correct for you, if you'd like. Personally, the only thing I'm missing is more content, maybe something about those anti-Abrahamic terrorists, to highlight the anomalous and bring some attention to the brewing conflict. I really it'd make the article bloated for some readers, so I'll leave the decision up to you, though I think it might gain you that desired meat mentioned by others in these comments. :)</p>
<p>Regardless, I like this one, and I'm glad to see more Sarkic stuff pop up. ^^</p>
<p>+1</p>

